[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue and one fix. Its reports hold three problems, and each
now has its own ticket:

| problem in #4471 | where the desk's table counts it | ticket |
|---|---|---|
| The shared parser reads dates month first | row `parser`, without the one-day moves | [#1](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/1) |
| The booking-v3 form hints MM/DD to day-first tenants | row `hint` | [#2](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/2) |
| Dates move by one day (time zone) | note under `parser`: read as a one-day move | [#3](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/3) |

<Callout kind="warn">
Not known, not one fix. The queued parser fix closes only #1. The booking-v3 hint (#2) and the
one-day moves (#3) stay broken after it ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds, as the desk counts it

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Each report is counted once, by its id. The one-day moves are counted where the desk files them,
under `parser`, and noted under the table. They are their own problem all the same: ticket #3 covers them, and ticket #1 does
not, so every report is in exactly one ticket.

## The three problems

### 1 · The shared parser reads dates month first · [#1](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/1)

Every tenant on file writes the day first, and the shared parser reads every date month first, so
day and month swap: "4 March turned into 3 April". It hits every tenant, through the app, by
email and through the booking-v2 form. This is the problem #4471 describes.

### 2 · The booking-v3 form hints MM/DD · [#2](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/2)

All of these reports came through the booking form of the three tenants on booking-v3
(alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour). The form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field,
so people type the month first, and the form then reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The
reports look like the parser's, but the cause is the hint. A parser fix does not touch it. The
table above marks this row "not this ticket — no ticket of its own": its ticket is now #2.

### 3 · Dates move by one day · [#3](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/3)

These reports name no swapped month. The date moves by one day: "Invite says Tuesday 12 May.
Calendar says Monday 11 May", "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday", "Every
booking in June is one day off", "The invite arrived before I made the booking". That is a
time-zone or day-boundary bug. The desk lists them as one-day moves (desk notes) and files them
under the parser by tenant, but a parser fix will not close them.

## Why they ended up in one ticket

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line. The same
  subjects, "Date is wrong" among them, occur in all three problems, so all three landed in #4471.
- The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser; the table above shows how often it
  disagrees with the cause. It cannot split the ticket.
- The split uses what the desk knows about the tenant (locale and booking form), the channel, and
  the desk's own notes on one-day moves.

## What to do

- Track each problem in its own ticket: [#1](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/1),
  [#2](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/2),
  [#3](https://github.com/promanowicz/megadev/issues/3).
- Change the status of #4471 from known to split, and point it to this page.
- Before the next merge on subject, check the tenant and the channel: two reports with the same
  subject can have different causes.

